  "reason": "The same work and essentially the same change are already saved in decisions.md as item 3, 'Monthly search of Houston books for Enron Canada (ECC) deals' ($364.65 a month), which cites the same Giron messages (108, 114, 195, 292, 360, 407) and already books every ECC counterparty to FT-US/CAND-ERMS automatically with a daily list of deals that slip through.",
  "research": null
}

{
  "name": "Gathering P&L top pages and curve-shift reports for Arthur Andersen's monthly gas testing",
  "today": "Each month Arthur Andersen (Sharon Smith, Mark Austin) emails the gas controllers (Kelly, Keiser, Giron, Baumbach and later the book admins too) a list of regions. For each region they want the P&L top page for the last day of the month and, where curve shift drives the P&L, top pages and curve-shift reports for five of the largest days. Each controller forwards the request to his book admins, who find and copy the reports and send them back up or have AA come and collect copies. The reports already exist in the risk system every day; the cost is finding, copying and routing them. It stalls when the controller is away (Giron in Chicago, AA asking for someone else), when a controller changes job (a second request reaches Gossett after Giron took over the West desk), when items are not sent (AA chasing three missing regions to close its third-quarter file), and when AA cannot tell who owns which desk.",
  "change": "A month-end job saves every gas book's top pages and curve-shift reports into a dated read-only folder AA can open, with a list of each book's owner.",
  "explanation": "At each month-end close a scheduled job copies the official last-day P&L top page and the daily top pages and curve-shift reports for every gas book into a dated, read-only folder that Arthur Andersen can open (a shared drive, since AA lost Enron Lotus Notes access from 28 February 2001). The folder also holds a list of which book admin and controller own each book. AA takes its sample straight from the folder and contacts the listed owner only to discuss what drove the P&L. Controllers no longer forward the request, admins no longer find and copy reports, and second requests and 'come get the copies' calls stop. The driver discussions stay as they are and are not counted.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/583.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the top sheets relating to the following desk:  West Firm, \nNorth West Firm, Central Firm, Texas Intra-Month, and Central Intra-Month."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/516.eml",
      "quote": "In order for us to complete our monthly gas testing, please provide the \nfollowing items."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/420.eml",
      "quote": "we have not received the P&L top pages \nor curve shift reports for the following regions:  West Firm, FT Northwest \nand Mgmt. West."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/327.eml",
      "quote": "We are requesting that you supply the P & L top pages for the \nlast day of the month for those regions that are applicable to you."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/299.eml",
      "quote": "please direct me to the individual responsible \nfor each of the desks listed below."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/201.eml",
      "quote": "As part of our monthly testing, we review the monthly Natural Gas P & L \nStatement and identify specific regions for which we would like to review \nadditional documentation."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/516.eml",
      "quote": "Please get this info to me and I will pass it on to AA.",
      "note": "The controller relays the request to four admins and the reports come back through him: the forwarding chain the folder removes. This request covers eight region-months (two for August, six for September)."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/516.eml",
      "quote": "if the majority of \nthe P&L pertains to curve shift, please provide the P&L top pages for five \nof  the largest days including the Curve Shift Reports.",
      "note": "Each region can need six or more reports pulled, not one page, which is where the admins' time goes."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/317.eml",
      "quote": "Is there someone else that can direct us to?  I would like to get this \ninformation as soon as it is possible.",
      "note": "The request stalls when the controller is travelling; Giron then forwards it to three admins and again to Kam Keiser. The Nov/Dec list in this request has 21 region-months."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/583.eml",
      "quote": "Darron has taken my position as west controller.  Please send him all future \nrequests for the west desk.",
      "note": "A second request is rerouted after a job change before anyone starts on it; an owner list in the folder would avoid this."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/420.eml",
      "quote": "Pull this together and then call Sharon so they can come get the copies.",
      "note": "Missing items are chased months later and handed over as paper copies collected in person."
    },
    {
      "file": "giron-d/sent/322.eml",
      "quote": "I forwarded this to Carole to take care of Northwest as she was running it \nNov and Dec.",
      "note": "Even among the admins the request is passed on again to whoever ran the book that month."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "month",
    "file": "giron-d/sent/201.eml",
    "quote": "As part of our monthly testing"
  },
  "minutes": 150
}

